LedgerSMB on FenrirOS
=====================

Code in /usr/share/ledgersmb, its CPAN libraries in /usr/lib/ledgersmb/perl5,
configuration in /etc/ledgersmb. The dinit service ledgersmb runs it under
Starman on localhost:5762 as the ledgersmb user; nginx serves the UI and
proxies the rest. `ledgersmb-admin` is its command-line administration.
PDF/PostScript output through LaTeX is not available (no TeX in FenrirOS);
HTML, CSV, ODS and XLS(X) output are.

1. PostgreSQL: install and start postgresql, then create the role LedgerSMB
   administers its company databases with (it needs CREATEDB and CREATEROLE):
     su -s /bin/sh postgres -c "createuser -S -d -r -l -P lsmb_dbadmin"
   (asks for its password).
2. cp /etc/ledgersmb/ledgersmb.yaml.sample /etc/ledgersmb/ledgersmb.yaml
   and review it (mail transport, printers, proxy_ip). Optionally
   ledgersmb.log.conf.sample as ledgersmb.log.conf.
3. dinitctl enable ledgersmb; nginx: /usr/share/doc/ledgersmb/nginx-ledgersmb.conf,
   dinitctl enable nginx.
4. Open https://<host>/setup.pl, log in as lsmb_dbadmin, create a company
   database and its first user; then use https://<host>/login.pl.
   (Or with ledgersmb-admin: ledgersmb-admin create, ledgersmb-admin user create.)
5. After an update of this package: open setup.pl for each company
   database to upgrade it, then dinitctl restart ledgersmb.
